{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md | tail -51'","aggregated_output":"   249\t- the whole read page, collapsed and with the card expanded, equals the frozen page from that dated package. The card holds its\n   250\t  question, status, \"Answer: Yes\", \"1 piece of evidence\", then its single evidence entry and source;\n   251\t- so the entry is visible, and nothing else is: neither judgement's explanation, nor \"around $1 trillion\", \"rung 4\" or \"at rung\".\n   252\t\n   253\t**The decisive negatives** (checks of the check). Each is a copy of the `old-1` page with its script changed and its CSP hash\n   254\trecomputed, so the changed script runs. Each must fail for its own reason:\n   255\t- **inside the card:** one visible line \"Forecast: $361 billion\" added in the `v8` card fails the comparison;\n   256\t- **beside the card:** the same line added just before the `v8` card, as its sibling, fails the comparison (it lands in `other`);\n   257\t- **transparent:** the whole list set to `opacity: 0` misses the 3 s deadline, because no card is visible, although every card\n   258\t  exists;\n   259\t- **clipped:** quotes held to one line (`white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis` added through the script's\n   260\t  inline style on each quote) fail the not-clipped rule at 390 px, although their text is identical;\n   261\t- **clipping wrapper:** each quote placed inside a one-line wrapper (`contain: paint; height: 1.5em`), the quote itself wrapping\n   262\t  normally, fails the clipping-ancestor rule at 390 px;\n   263\t- **unreadable marker:** in dark, the marker drawn in `--ink` on an `--ink` background (`color` set to `rgb(15, 20, 13)` through the\n   264\t  script's inline style) fails the contrast rule, although its text, box and opacity pass.\n   265\t\n   266\t**The escaping screen.** The fixture page of test 2, with that evidence expanded, shows the exact quote as text and has no `img`\n   267\telement.\n   268\t\n   269\t**The fetch mutant.**\n   270\t- **Setup:** a copy of the `old-1` page with `fetch(\"http://127.0.0.1:59999/library\")` added to its script, and the CSP script hash\n   271\t  recomputed for the altered script, so the script runs.\n   272\t- **It must fail the check for the right reason:**\n   273\t  - the normal list renders;\n   274\t  - a `Log.entryAdded` security error names `http://127.0.0.1:59999/library` and `connect-src`.\n   275\t\n   276\t  A page whose script is blocked wholesale does not earn the credit.\n   277\t- **Measured on this Mac (Chrome 158, headless, scratchpad probe):** a CSP-blocked fetch produces no `Network.requestWillBeSent`. It\n   278\t  produces a `security` error naming the address and the directive, and a `javascript` error.\n   279\t- **The probe page named port 8788.** Chrome refused it under the CSP before connecting (\"Refused to connect\"), so no request reached\n   280\t  that service. Port 59999 is not on the fetch specification's blocked-port list, and nothing listens there.\n   281\t\n   282\t**Phone width and dark scheme.**\n   283\t- **At 390 × 844** (`Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride`):\n   284\t  - `document.scrollingElement.scrollWidth` is at most 390;\n   285\t  - with `v8` expanded, the whole read page, with the not-clipped rule, equals the frozen expanded page;\n   286\t  - Morningstar's quote (`e2295`), scrolled into view, wraps over more than one line (`getClientRects` on its text), and its box lies\n   287\t    within the 390 px viewport.\n   288\t- With `Emulation.setEmulatedMedia` `prefers-color-scheme: dark`, the body's computed background is exactly `rgb(15, 20, 13)` (the\n   289\t  shared `--ink`, used as the dark page colour). In light, it is `rgb(245, 242, 235)` (`--paper`).\n   290\t\n   291\t**Budget,** set before the first control:\n   292\t- at most 3 s for the `old-1` page in headless Chrome, from `Page.navigate` until the full list is visible: the fallback line is\n   293\t  gone, and every expected question's card is present and passes the same visibility test as the text;\n   294\t- the page's size at most the data's bytes plus 64 KB.\n   295\t\n   296\t## 7. Prior decisions\n   297\t\n   298\tD726, D756, D757, D758, D759; council 74 (no idea input); council 75d (literal expected values); D690 (poc-v118 stays the product);\n   299\tD163 (English product text).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
