{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'template|colour|contrast|wrapper|hash' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round76g-brief.md; rg -n 'Morningstar|v36|v10|sha256|accepted' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md | head -22\"","aggregated_output":"7:transparency, a clipping wrapper, the same colour on the same background. Revision 6 answers 76f with three general rules instead of\n10:- a WCAG AA contrast floor for every read text;\n11:- a pinned template, so the screen run certifies one exact template and any change must be re-certified.\n18:2. Is there any remaining way, within the pinned template (`page == render_page(data)`, byte for byte, with the template's style\n19:   and script hashes fixed in the tests), for the shipped page to leak, make a request, or show the reader something other than the\n21:3. **Convergence (AGENTS §1 and §5).** The template is fixed and pinned. An adversarial CSS change can enter only through a template\n22:   change, which fails the pinned hashes. If what remains is a further possible tightening of the screen check against templates\n3:**Result: accepted by council 75g** (`codex-r75g.md`), after rounds 75 to 75f. Slice 1 is built to `RELEASE-BUILD.md`:\n24:| Ten text fields accepted null, which revision 10 forbids | strings only | test 23; mutant \"null accepted as text\" |\n52:| The check script accepted an example id whose text had changed | superseded by council 75d's rule below | this run |\n56:- test 21 accepted a partial report;\n124:  - Morningstar's $361 billion (`e2295`, under `v8`);\n135:  - `old-3/v36` at 2026-08-25 (judgement 799) and `old-1/v10` at 2026-08-28 (judgement 865) are the latest judgements there, and\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D75[689]|\"'^## 0'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | tail -25; head -40 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:12:## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:448:**The one next task: slice 2 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release, the reader's screen (D758 order; D756's screen check).** The release\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:453:**Slice 1 is built and accepted at $0 (D759).**\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:471:The record of the D758 step:\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:473:**Earlier next task (done, D759): build slice 1 once its design passes council 74 (D758).**\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:477:**Earlier next task (done, D758): Alex chooses whether to open release work, and what non-number questions show (D757).** Decided by\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:478:council 73 under D439 (D758): open, and (a).\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:480:The record of the D756 step:\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:482:**Earlier next task (done, D757): when release work opens, a $0 check of the reader's screen for number questions (D756).** On a\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:486:- **Alex closed the v13s judge line at its STOP** (D756: end the line, release with \"Forecast unavailable\"). Nothing from it enters the\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:492:**Earlier next task (done, D756): Alex reads the paid re-send's STOP (D755) and confirms the council's recommendation.** The\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11823:## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11845:  unavailable\" (D756). D726 says it \"is built with the release work, which is not started\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11867:## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \"Forecast unavailable\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11870:  Production 方向去走了\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \"同意\"; D756 \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\"). D757 left two\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11880:     code, the line is closed (D756), and the STOP bars tuning on the 36 answers. The findings stay on record.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11881:  4. **Order:** the exporter and the checked package first; the reader's screen second (it completes D756's screen check). How the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11885:## D759 · 2026-11-23 · Slice 1 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release is built and accepted at $0 (councils 74–74j design, 75–75g build); nothing committed or published\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11887:- **Under D439 and D758.** Release work was opened by council 73 (D758). This slice carries it out locally at $0. Nothing is\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11895:    Yes/No question carries its question, evidence and answer labels (D758 §4 a);\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11926:  - slice 2, the release page that reads only the package, with a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen (D756's screen check);\n# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n   word for it is already given.\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\n\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\nany one step's own score.\n\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
