{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md | sed -n '116,148p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round76g-brief.md\"","aggregated_output":"   116\t- **How the evidence is counted.** The count includes each piece once per question that holds it. Every piece has exactly one source\n   117\t  row (`old-1`: 5,390 rows for 5,390 pieces).\n   118\t- **The script exits non-zero when any check it names fails:** each store's day, classes and evidence; the budgets; each example; each\n   119\t  exact refusal; the forged value's identity; `v8`; each leak; the control; the closing. This run ended \"every acceptance item and\n   120\t  budget met\".\n   121\t\n   122\t**The decisive acceptance case** (council 74, `old-1`):\n   123\t- **Kept, each equal to the store and to its full text written into the script before the run:**\n   124\t  - Morningstar's $361 billion (`e2295`, under `v8`);\n   125\t  - the genuine \"Bullish confirmation\" quote (`e1865`, under `v4`, `v5`, `v8`);\n   126\t  - the analysts' \"$390 billion\" (`e3597`, under `v4`, `v5`).\n   127\t- **The system's own forecast** (`j1580` implied outcome, \"About $390 billion: …\"):\n   128\t  - substituted into `e2295`'s summary, it is refused with exactly \"question v8.evidence e2295.one_line: differs from the store\";\n   129\t  - added to the manifest, it is refused with exactly \"the manifest: keys off the allow-list ['note'], missing []\".\n   130\t\n   131\t**The other checks:**\n   132\t- **`old-1/v8`:** class `number`, marked \"Forecast unavailable\". Its 1,284 pieces of evidence are the same ids as `service.evidence` at\n   133\t  the bound.\n   134\t- **The known Yes/No leaks at their own days.**\n   135\t  - `old-3/v36` at 2026-08-25 (judgement 799) and `old-1/v10` at 2026-08-28 (judgement 865) are the latest judgements there, and\n   136\t    each package carries its own day (3,239 and 5,673 pieces of evidence).\n   137\t  - Both keep \"Yes\".\n   138\t  - The full explanation and reason texts are absent.\n   139\t  - So are the judgements' own phrases: \"around $1 trillion\", \"rung 4\", \"at rung\" and \"capex at rung\" occur in no field.\n   140\t- **Control:** event `old-1/v3` keeps \"Yes\" and its evidence, equal to the store.\n   141\t- **Closing,** on a copy of `old-1` with a closing switch for `v8`, \"due 2026-09-20, frozen on 2026-09-20 at rung 2 Bullish\":\n   142\t  - `bundle.view_bundle` exposes it;\n   143\t  - the package shows `open: false`;\n   144\t  - the reason appears nowhere.\n   145\t  - The word \"Bullish\" does occur inside six `v8` fields: five source titles and the genuine `e1865` quote. That is source wording,\n   146\t    which the design keeps.\n   147\t\n   148\t## 3. The diagnostic search, every hit read\n     1\t# Council round 76g: the slice-2 design, revision 6 (read-only)\n     2\t\n     3\tYou are an independent reviewer. Do not edit any file. The repository is /Users/lchingen/hivemind. Cite file:line.\n     4\t\n     5\t`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md` is at revision 6. Rounds 76 to 76f each found no leak and no request path.\n     6\tTheir remaining findings were ways the screen check could certify a page the reader cannot fully read: clipping, an extra line,\n     7\ttransparency, a clipping wrapper, the same colour on the same background. Revision 6 answers 76f with three general rules instead of\n     8\tone patch per trick (AGENTS §1):\n     9\t- no clipping ancestor;\n    10\t- a WCAG AA contrast floor for every read text;\n    11\t- a pinned template, so the screen run certifies one exact template and any change must be re-certified.\n    12\t\n    13\tThe governing documents are the same as in `round76-brief.md`.\n    14\t\n    15\t## Questions\n    16\t\n    17\t1. Are the two 76f findings closed, as classes, by the general rules? Name any still open, with its line.\n    18\t2. Is there any remaining way, within the pinned template (`page == render_page(data)`, byte for byte, with the template's style\n    19\t   and script hashes fixed in the tests), for the shipped page to leak, make a request, or show the reader something other than the\n    20\t   frozen screen?\n    21\t3. **Convergence (AGENTS §1 and §5).** The template is fixed and pinned. An adversarial CSS change can enter only through a template\n    22\t   change, which fails the pinned hashes. If what remains is a further possible tightening of the screen check against templates\n    23\t   that cannot ship, list it as optional and give the verdict accordingly.\n    24\t4. Verdict: ready to build, or not ready with each serious finding.\n    25\t\n    26\t**Out of scope:**\n    27\t- the frozen pieces;\n    28\t- the closed v13s line;\n    29\t- slice 1's accepted internals;\n    30\t- the idea path;\n    31\t- the evidence-summary disagreement;\n    32\t- wording.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
